note.paragraph:
An efficient way to compute a $B\text{-matrix}$ $P^{- 1}AP$ is to compute $AP$ and then to row reduce the augmented matrix $\left\lbrack \begin{array}{rr}
        P & {AP}
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$ to $\left\lbrack \begin{array}{rr}
        I & {P^{- 1}AP}
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$. A separate computation of $P^{- 1}$ is unnecessary. See Exercise 22 in Section 2.2.

